From d53b4837fd898afda9dd3510df9eaf162803faf3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Aniket Randive <arandive@qti.qualcomm.com>
Date: Mon, 8 Sep 2025 15:56:01 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 12/12] i2c: Enable multi random write feature

Enable multi-random write feature and add changes to
process IEOB IRQ for CDM mode. Enable only IEOB IRQ
for CDM mode. Make CCU QUP driver static to resolve
cyclic dependency issues between I2C, GSI, and CCU
drivers. Move invocation of SCM call to load QUP FW
from CCU QUP driver probe to GSI driver probe due
to symbol availability issues.

Change-Id: I5c31587c30a7410218d3b04e68f7226bad58bf6c
Signed-off-by: Aniket Randive <arandive@qti.qualcomm.com>
---
 drivers/dma/qcom/gpi.c                | 14 +++++----
 drivers/i2c/busses/i2c-qcom-geni.c    | 45 ++++++++++-----------------
 drivers/soc/qcom/qcom_ccu_qup.c       | 45 ++++++++++++++-------------
 include/linux/soc/qcom/qcom_ccu_qup.h |  5 ++-
 4 files changed, 53 insertions(+), 56 deletions(-)

